                        "entry_id": "4aaeadc6-5e23-3e65-bb22-4cb2e28ed821",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An unattractive or ugly thing or person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac05c20a-ba10-453f-9062-19648242187a",
                                "sense_id": "996faf53-1d7c-360a-8f50-2cefc443e0c7",
                                "text": "1982, United Press International, \"Clearly, an ugly dog\", 2 August.\nA hairless runt of a mutt named Chi-chi defeated them all in the 13th annual Ugliest Dog in the World contest: such unlovelies as the moth-eaten chow and the bulldog with a bad eye."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c449944c-4178-4072-a83b-b55a424a07a5",
                                "sense_id": "996faf53-1d7c-360a-8f50-2cefc443e0c7",
                                "text": "But the uptake of Irish studies by a range of migrant unlovelies clearly involves their expressing a quality of interest in the subject distinguishable from the harmless \"inherent interest\" which she so values and which presumably is palpable to \"anybody\", other than them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "507e21b3-8881-4e46-9660-d3c2738968fe",
                                "sense_id": "996faf53-1d7c-360a-8f50-2cefc443e0c7",
                                "text": "Many intriguing unlovelies are found in “The Boxtrolls,” a new 3-D animated fable that lifts liberally from the sketches and dark sensibility of Alan Snow’s creepy-good children’s novel “Here Be Monsters.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
